  "scope": "The actual320-slot program enumerates the row positions through real binary increment/reversal, then passes that actual list and the original cost row into the unchanged positive inventory/minimum machine. No vertex labels, selected index, minimum value or size bound is supplied. The original optional minimumPositive output is exact, including earliest ties, retained original raw cost pointers and generated original index words. The selected_index/selected_valid corollaries derive valid original positions and an original-row-length word bound. The same physical run preserves the original cost row/source and pays its halt under a bound in the original row length and padded fraction fields. Original input representation, H/A and dense cursor remain premises. Subsequent minimum-to-lambda/shifted-row composition and complete guess/solver remain separate. Twelve physical cases independently specify the chosen original occurrence and exact raw costs/indices.",
